{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.WordFiltrationObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WordFiltrationObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Quotient.Operations","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WordFiltration.gbDepth_not_from_single_stratum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WordFiltration.gbDepth_not_from_single_stratum","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WordFiltrationObstruction.lean#L109-L133","doc":"**The ideal-power filtration cannot carry the partition grading.**\n\nFormally: any function `d` on Young diagrams that is read off a filtration whose\ngraded pieces above degree `0` all vanish is *constant* on the diagrams that\nappear — but `gbDepth` is not constant on the partitions of `4`.\n\nStated as the implication rather than as a bare `≠` so that the hypothesis is\nvisible: what a filtration with one nonzero stratum can supply is a *constant*,\nand `gbDepth` is not one.\n\n**The step from `map_pow_eq_bot` to this theorem's `hconst` is prose, not\nLean.** Closing it in Lean would need `Z(H_n(q))` and the central idempotents\n`e_λ` as actual Lean objects, so that \"the grading `Z^{(k)}` read off the\nfiltration\" is a definition rather than a description; neither exists in the\ntree. So the two halves are each proved and the join between them is an\nargument — which is exactly the epistemic status the audit assigns to the\nbridge itself, and it would be dishonest to present this file as more. The real\ncontent is `gbDepth_ne_on_H4`; this theorem is the connector, and it is cheap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WordFiltration.graded_piece_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WordFiltration.graded_piece_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WordFiltrationObstruction.lean#L98-L103","doc":"**The associated graded is concentrated in degree `0`.** Every graded piece\n`J^k / J^{k+1}` with `k ≥ 1` is the zero quotient, since both terms are `⊥`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WordFiltration.map_pow_eq_bot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WordFiltration.map_pow_eq_bot","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WordFiltrationObstruction.lean#L91-L96","doc":"**Every positive power of the image vanishes.** So the filtration\n`J^k := π(I)^k` has `J^0 = A/I` and `J^k = 0` for all `k ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WordFiltration.map_defining_ideal_eq_bot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WordFiltration.map_defining_ideal_eq_bot","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WordFiltrationObstruction.lean#L83-L89","doc":"The image of the defining ideal in the quotient is zero.\n\nNot deep — it is what \"quotient by `I`\" means — but it is the whole obstruction,\nand stating it is what stops the free route being taken by accident. ","signatureChunk":0}]}